# HullTrend Telegram credentials
#
# Copy this file to your terminal's data folder as:
#     MQL5\Files\telegram.ini
# and fill in the two values below.
#
# This file is READ AT RUNTIME and is never compiled into an .ex5.
# Keep the real telegram.ini out of git - it is a credential.
#
# --- how to get the two values -------------------------------------
# token    : message @BotFather on Telegram, /newbot, copy the token
#            WHOLE. It has TWO halves joined by a colon:
#                <bot_id>:<secret>
#            e.g. 123456789:AAF-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#            The numeric half in front of the colon is PART OF THE
#            TOKEN. It is NOT the chat_id - it is the bot's own id,
#            and a bot cannot message itself. Splitting the token
#            across the two keys breaks both of them at once.
# chat_id  : add the bot to the target chat, send it any message, then
#            open in a browser:
#              https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates
#            and read result[0].message.chat.id
#            Personal chats are positive, groups/channels negative
#            (e.g. -1001234567890).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# One more step, outside this file: whitelist the API host in
#     Tools > Options > Expert Advisors > Allow WebRequest for listed URL
# add:  https://api.telegram.org
# Without it every send fails with error 5203 / status -1.

token   = PASTE_YOUR_BOT_TOKEN_HERE
chat_id = PASTE_YOUR_CHAT_ID_HERE
